Subject: [PATCH] Select the OpenSSL crypto implementation for SONiC Kerberos
Origin: SONiC sonic-fips src/krb5.patch/90-support-openssl-crypto-impl.patch
Upstream-Status: SONiC build configuration

Use SONiC OpenSSL for Kerberos cryptography, matching the existing FIPS
package recipe. Refresh only surrounding Debian-rule context for 1.21.3-5:
the multiarch libdir option was replaced upstream by the LMDB option.
The added configure flag remains unchanged.

diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
index 915528050..cbf03a206 100755
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ override_dh_auto_configure:
 	--with-system-verto \
 	--with-lmdb \
 		--sysconfdir=/etc  \
+		--with-crypto-impl=openssl \
 		--localstatedir=/etc
 
 override_dh_auto_build:
